$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Suzuki Cross-Coupling Reaction of Compound 5af 2 To compound 5ad (50 mg,
0.142 mmol) in dioxane (6.0 ml) were added Pd(PPh3)2Cl2 (10 mg, 0.1
equiv), 4-methoxy phenyl boronic acid (65 mg, 3.0 equiv), Cs2CO3 (277.6
mg, 6.0 equiv). After the mixture was stirred at room temperature for 30
min, H2O (1.0 ml) was added, and the reaction mixture was heated to
reflux for 30 h. After it was cooled to room temperature, the aqueous
layer was separated and extracted with ethyl acetate (25 ml ×2). The
combined organic layer was washed with brine, dried over anhydrous
Na2SO4, separated, and concentrated under reduced pressure to get crude
product, which was purified by flash column chromatography (hexanes/ethyl
acetate: 9/1). Compound 5af (45 mg, 84%). The ee was determined on a
Daicel Chiralpak IB column with hexanes : 2-propanol = 90 : 10, flow =
0.5 ml/min. (S)-tert-butyl
3-(4-(4-methoxyphenyl)-1H-pyrazol-1-yl)-3-phenylpropanoate (5af):
Retention times: 10.09 min [(R)-enantiomer], 13.65 min [(S)-enantiomer].
99% ee. FTIR (Neat) 2974, 2931, 1727, 1571, 1502, 1449, 1369, 1250, 1152,
1079, 1033, 955, 833, 746 cm-1. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ (ppm) 7.75 (s,
1H), 7.58 (s, 1H), 7.40–7.27 (m, 7H), 6.91–6.85 (m, 2H), 5.77 (dd, J =
6.2, 9.2 Hz, 1H), 3.80 (s, 3H), 3.50 (dd, J = 9.2, 15.9 Hz, 1H), 3.07
(dd, J = 6.2, 15.9 Hz, 1H), 1.34 (s, 9H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
(ppm) 169.4, 158.3, 139.6, 136.5, 128.8, 128.2, 126.8, 126.6, 125.4,
125.2 122.7, 114.2, 81.2, 62.3, 55.3, 41.6, 27.8. HRMS (ESI): calcd for
[C23H26N2O3+H]+ 379.2016, found 379.2015 [M+H]+.
